# Copy to .env and fill in. The real .env is git-ignored.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# Read by Spring through `spring.config.import` in application.properties, which
# is why this is Java .properties syntax rather than shell: no quotes around
# values, no `export`, and a literal backslash must be doubled.
#
# On a server you do not need this file at all -- set the same names as real
# environment variables instead (systemd `Environment=` or `EnvironmentFile=`).
# Environment variables take precedence over anything in .env, so a stray file
# left on a host cannot quietly override the service's own configuration.
#
# Both values are optional. Left empty the app still starts, and degrades:
# the City feed falls back to unauthenticated access and the dark basemap asks
# for unkeyed tiles.

# City of Winnipeg Open Data (Socrata) application token.
# Without one, requests are unauthenticated and share a much lower rate limit.
# Register at https://data.winnipeg.ca/profile/edit/developer_settings
WFPS_CITY_API_TOKEN=

# CARTO basemap key, sent with the dark-mode tiles. CARTO's basemaps stopped
# serving unkeyed raster requests, so dark mode needs this to draw.
# Register at https://carto.com/
WFPS_MAP_TILES_KEY=
